        ("What does role='presentation' or role='none' do?", "It removes semantic meaning from an element (e.g., table used for legacy layout), exposing only its raw text content to screen readers.", "Advanced", "Accessibility", "<table role=\"presentation\">...</table>", "Does it hide text from the screen reader?"),
        ("Why should link text like 'Click Here' or 'Read More' be avoided?", "Screen reader users often browse by link lists out of context; 'Click Here' gives zero information on where the link leads.", "Intermediate", "Accessibility", "<a href=\"/pricing\">View Developer Pricing</a> <!-- PREFERRED -->", "How can you provide screen-reader-only context?"),
