        ("What happens if you have duplicate ID attributes on the same page?", "Invalid HTML. document.getElementById() will only return the first element, breaking scripts, styles, and label associations.", "Intermediate", "Debugging", "<div id=\"box\"></div>\n<div id=\"box\"></div> <!-- BUG: Duplicate ID -->", "What should you use instead of duplicate IDs?"),
        ("Why should inline styles (<div style='...'>) be avoided in production HTML?", "Inline styles mix presentation with structure, defeat CSS caching, increase HTML file size, and violate strict Content Security Policy (CSP).", "Intermediate", "Scenario", "", "When are inline styles acceptable?"),
        ("What is Content Security Policy (CSP) in HTML?", "CSP is a security standard configured via HTTP headers or <meta> tags that prevents Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) by restricting allowed script sources.", "Advanced", "Security", "<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src 'self'\">", "Can CSP disallow inline scripts?"),
