        ("What is clickjacking and how does the X-Frame-Options header prevent it?", "Clickjacking tricks users into clicking invisible iframes. X-Frame-Options: DENY or SAMEORIGIN prevents other sites from embedding your page in iframes.", "Advanced", "Security", "X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN", "What CSP directive replaces X-Frame-Options?"),
        ("What does the 'crossorigin' attribute do on <link> and <script>?", "It controls whether Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) headers are sent when requesting external assets like fonts or CDN scripts.", "Advanced", "Practical", "<link rel=\"preload\" href=\"font.woff2\" as=\"font\" crossorigin>", "What happens if crossorigin is missing on preloaded fonts?"),
        ("What does Subresource Integrity (SRI) do on <script> tags?", "The 'integrity' attribute contains a cryptographic hash of the script. The browser refuses to execute the script if a CDN was tampered with.", "Advanced", "Security", "<script src=\"https://cdn.example.com/lib.js\" integrity=\"sha384-...\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>", "What happens if the hash doesn't match?"),
        ("Why should you avoid using obsolete tags like <center>, <font>, and <marquee>?", "They were deprecated in HTML5 because presentation belongs in CSS. They lack semantic meaning and harm modern maintainability.", "Easy", "Concept", "<!-- AVOID --> <font color=\"red\">Text</font>\n<!-- USE --> <span class=\"text-error\">Text</span>", "How do you achieve marquee effect in modern CSS?"),
        ("What does the 'contenteditable' attribute do in HTML?", "The contenteditable boolean attribute makes any HTML element directly editable by the user in the browser window.", "Intermediate", "Practical", "<div contenteditable=\"true\">Click here to edit text</div>", "What does document.execCommand do with contenteditable?"),
        ("What does the 'spellcheck' attribute do?", "The spellcheck attribute specifies whether the browser should check spelling and grammar in text fields and editable elements.", "Easy", "Practical", "<textarea spellcheck=\"true\"></textarea>", "Can you turn spellcheck off on code inputs?"),
        ("What is the purpose of the <dialog> method showModal() vs show()?", "showModal() opens the dialog as a top-layer modal that blocks background interaction and adds a dark ::backdrop. show() opens a non-modal dialog.", "Advanced", "Comparison", "dialogEl.showModal(); // Modal\ndialogEl.show(); // Non-modal", "How do you close a dialog in HTML?"),
        ("How do you close an HTML5 <dialog> with a form?", "Use <form method='dialog'><button>Close</button></form>. Submitting closes the dialog automatically without JavaScript.", "Advanced", "Practical", "<dialog>\n  <form method=\"dialog\"><button>Close</button></form>\n</dialog>", "What is dialog.returnValue?"),
        ("What causes the 'Flash of Unstyled Content' (FOUC)?", "FOUC occurs when HTML renders before external CSS finishes downloading and parsing, momentarily showing raw unstyled content.", "Intermediate", "Scenario", "", "How does placing CSS in the head prevent FOUC?"),
        ("What is a web component Custom Element in HTML?", "A custom element allows developers to define new HTML tags (like <user-card>) with custom behaviors extending HTMLElement.", "Advanced", "Concept", "customElements.define('user-card', UserCard);", "Why must custom element tag names have a hyphen?"),
